  he has to go resolve himself is a decision he defers.

The five: prefix-tolerant + case-insensitive; resolve by MAX never by position; search root AND
  every worktree per slug; max across copies; prefer root on disagreement (verdicts are authored
  on main, so a worktree copy is inherited or stale).

Adopted vc-f5's causal framing wholesale instead of listing bugs: four readers of one field, one
  day, two sessions, all four wrong, each written by whoever had just fixed the previous one --
  and the cause is TWO UNMODELLED FACTS, not four mistakes. Writers do not guarantee position,
  and this repo is never a single checkout. A reader modelling both is correct; a reader fixing
  one symptom becomes the next ledger row, which is what happened four times. That framing is now
  in the gate as the rationale, because it is the difference between a fix and a fifth reader.

vc-f5 also repaired its own reconciler rather than leaving it as the fourth bad reader on the
  grounds that it was about to be superseded. Worth recording as a good call: "it will be
  replaced" is how a broken safety net survives. It now resolves t-010 as c3-FAIL from its own
